@*
    NotFoundPage rather than the <NotFound> fragment: under static server rendering the fragment is
    never rendered, so every mistyped URL was answered with a 404 and an empty body while this copy
    sat here looking as though it were the site's answer. The page is routable, which is what the
    parameter takes, and it is the same answer whether the route did not match or a page decided
    there was nothing at it.
*@
<Router AppAssembly="typeof(Program).Assembly" NotFoundPage="typeof(MUI.Web.Components.Pages.NotFound)">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="typeof(MainLayout)" />
    </Found>
</Router>
